WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.720
Speaker 1: Does MAGA care more about democracy&nbsp;
or gas prices? Or maybe more accurately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:15.300
does MAGA care more about democracy or the promise&nbsp;
of lower gas prices when the current gas prices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:23.940
aren't even very high? A version of this question&nbsp;
is what Chauncey Vega asks in a very good new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:32.220
commentary in Salon called Is America Ready To&nbsp;
Trade Democracy for Cheap Gas? That's fascism in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:38.940
a nutshell. Americans understand rates, Chauncey,&nbsp;
that democracy is in dire peril. That doesn't mean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:44.700
they believe in it or give a damn. I encourage&nbsp;
you to check out this piece written yesterday.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:51.600
He references the New York Times headline,&nbsp;
which says Voters see democracy in peril,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:58.740
but saving it isn't a priority. He writes, The&nbsp;
details are grim. Voters, quote, overwhelmingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:04.260
believe American democracy is under threat but&nbsp;
seem remarkably apathetic about that danger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:10.380
with relatively few calling it the nation's&nbsp;
most pressing problem. More than one third of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:14.280
independent voters in the poll said they were&nbsp;
open to supporting candidates who reject the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:21.300
legitimacy of the 2020 election because economic&nbsp;
concerns are more urgent. 71% agreed democracy was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:28.500
at risk. Only 7% said it was the most important&nbsp;
problem in the country. So one of the important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:34.920
things to consider is that for many of these MAGA&nbsp;
voters, it's the promise of lower gas prices,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.420
which they're willing to trade for democracy,&nbsp;
for the will of the people, depending who is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:45.600
in office. But when you look at gas prices, you&nbsp;
say they're not even really that high. They're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:52.980
down like 30 something percent from the peak. And&nbsp;
for the average vehicle, even if they were to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.980 --> 00:02:00.540
down another 30%, you're only talking about quite&nbsp;
literally a few dollars difference for every full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:08.220
tank that couldn't really be worth trading for a&nbsp;
functioning democracy, could it? But it appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:16.500
that for many voters, indeed it is. And so we are&nbsp;
down to the very end here as it comes to the 2022&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:22.440
midterms. We're going to have results starting&nbsp;
Tuesday night, and I hope you'll be live with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:27.660
me on YouTube, Twitch and Facebook. The 2022&nbsp;
midterms may be just the beginning. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:33.840
they almost certainly will be just the beginning.&nbsp;
We will probably learn in the 24 to 48 hours that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:43.440
follow Tuesday's elections. If and how committed&nbsp;
are right wingers to democracy 2020 suggested? The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:49.860
answer is not particularly committed, but we will&nbsp;
see very quickly are they doing this? If we won,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:54.780
it was fair. But if we lost, it's rigged thing.&nbsp;
Are they going to do it again? And if they do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.780 --> 00:03:02.040
it will be a sign that it is now just sop standard&nbsp;
operating procedure for these folks and that will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:11.280
be yet another divot in the democracy that is left&nbsp;
at this point in time. I don't know that they do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:18.600
care about democracy at this point anymore. I&nbsp;
think that at this point they just want to win&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:26.700
now. We also just want to win, but we want to win&nbsp;
by people realizing their ideas are a disaster.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:34.200
We're not trying to win by just putting in office&nbsp;
people who got fewer votes. That is a critical,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:40.920
fundamental difference. You might think the top&nbsp;
tax rate should be 38% and you might think it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:48.120
42 and I might think it's 43. And those are&nbsp;
reasonable differences that exist in reality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:55.980
But if one of us believes that actually if my&nbsp;
candidate gets fewer votes, we should figure out a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:02.220
way to install them anyway. That is very different&nbsp;
than a disagreement about tax policy or foreign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:10.500
policy or whatever the case may be. I. I hate&nbsp;
the fact that the answer to is America ready to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:16.620
give up democracy because they have been convinced&nbsp;
cheaper gas is more ex-pat, more important. I am&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:23.520
afraid that the answer is indeed yes. And we will&nbsp;
know much more about that, what, 72 hours from now

